Design a tri-state buffer circuit that controls the output based on an enable signal. When the enable signal is high, the output directly reflects the input. When the enable signal is low, the output goes to high-impedance (represented by 1'bz), effectively disconnecting the output from the input. The module also includes logic to maintain the previous output state when disabled, using a feedback mechanism to ensure the output can hold its value based on the input state when enabled.
