description:
Design a zero-to-one counter that increments a 4-bit output (`count`) each time a rising edge is detected on any of the first four bits of a 16-bit input (`in`). The counting mechanism triggers specifically when a bit transitions from low to high, ensuring that each pulse is counted only once per edge. The output reflects the total count of such transitions observed since the last clock cycle. The previous state of the input is stored in `prev_in` to facilitate edge detection.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input [15:0] in,
    output [3:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input [15:0] in,
    output [3:0] out
);reg [15:0] prev_in;
reg [3:0] count;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (in[0] && !prev_in[0]) begin
        count <= count + 1;
    end
    if (in[1] && !prev_in[1]) begin
        count <= count + 1;
    end
    if (in[2] && !prev_in[2]) begin
        count <= count + 1;
    end
    if (in[3] && !prev_in[3]) begin
        count <= count + 1;
    end
    prev_in <= in;
end

assign out = count;

endmodule

