description:
Implement a signed 4-bit Booth multiplier that calculates the product of two signed 4-bit inputs, A and B, producing an 8-bit signed output, Z. The design uses a combination of sequential logic to handle partial products based on the current and previous bits of B, applying the appropriate addition or subtraction according to Booth's algorithm. The resulting product is assigned to the output Z, effectively providing a mechanism for signed multiplication utilizing a bit-pairing approach to optimize the process.
module top_module(
    input signed [3:0] A,
    input signed [3:0] B,
    output signed [7:0] Z
);

code:
module top_module(
    input signed [3:0] A,
    input signed [3:0] B,
    output signed [7:0] Z
);wire signed [7:0] product;
    reg signed [8:0] partial;
    reg [1:0] bit_pair;
    integer i;

    assign product = A * B;

    always @(*) begin
        if (B[0] == 0 && bit_pair == 2'b01) begin
            partial = partial - A;
        end else if (B[0] == 1 && bit_pair == 2'b10) begin
            partial = partial + A;
        end
        bit_pair <= {B[0], B[1]};
        partial = partial >> 1;
    end

    assign Z = partial[7:0];

endmodule

