Design a circuit that outputs a HIGH signal only when all four input signals (in1, in2, in3, in4) are LOW. In all other cases, the output will be LOW. This module functions as a detector for the condition where all inputs are zero, effectively serving as a simple all-zeroes checker.
module top_module(
    input in1, in2, in3, in4,
    output out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input in1, in2, in3, in4,
    output out
);reg out_reg;

    always @(*) begin
        case ({in1, in2, in3, in4})
            {1'b0, 1'b0, 1'b0, 1'b0}: out_reg = 1'b1;
            default: out_reg = 1'b0;
        endcase
    end

    assign out = out_reg;

endmodule

