description:
Implement the Verilog module based on the following description.
You are given a 12-bit input vector d[11:0]. We want to perform some operations on the input vector: 
// (1) out_sum: Each bit of this output vector should indicate the sum of the corresponding input bit and its neighbour to the right modulo 2. For example, out_sum[2] should indicate if d[2] + d[1] is 1. Since d[0] has no neighbour to the right, the answer is obvious so we don't need to know out_sum[0]. 
// (2) out_and: Each bit of this output vector should indicate whether both the corresponding input bit and its neighbour to the left are '1'. For example, out_and[10] should indicate if d[10] and d[11] are both 1. Since d[11] has no neighbour to the left, the answer is obvious so we don't need to know out_and[11]. 
// (3) out_xor: Each bit of this output vector should indicate whether the corresponding input bit is different from its neighbour to the left. For example, out_xor[10] should indicate if d[10] is different from d[11]. For this part, treat the vector as wrapping around, so d[11]'s neighbour to the left is d[0].

module top_module (
	input [11:0] d,
	output [10:0] out_sum,
	output [10:0] out_and,
	output [11:0] out_xor);

code:
module top_module (
	input [11:0] d,
	output [10:0] out_sum,
	output [10:0] out_and,
	output [11:0] out_xor);assign out_sum = d[10:0] + d[11:1];
	assign out_and = d[10:0] & d[11:1];
	assign out_xor = d ^ {d[0], d[11:1]};

endmodule

