description:
Design a digital circuit that behaves as a dual-output multiplexer with selective routing based on a 2-bit selection input. The module has three single-bit inputs (in0, in1, in2) and produces two outputs (out1 and out2). When the selection signal (sel) is 00, out1 is assigned the value of in1 and out2 is assigned the value of in0. For selection values of 01, 10, and 11, out1 is set to in2 while out2 remains driven by in1. This design facilitates the selection of inputs based on the sel value, allowing versatile control of output states.
module top_module(

             out1, out2,

             sel, in0, in1, in2
             );

code:
module top_module(

             out1, out2,

             sel, in0, in1, in2
             );input [1:0] sel;
   input       in0, in1, in2;

   output      out1;
   output      out2;

   reg         out1;
   reg         out2;


   always @ (in0 or in1 or in2 or sel)
     if (sel == 2'b00)
       begin
          out1 = in1;
          out2 = in0;
       end
     else
       begin
          out1 = in2;
          out2 = in1;
       end


   always @ (in1 or in2 or sel)
     if (sel == 2'b00)
       out1 = in1;
     else
       out1 = in2;

endmodule

