description:
Design a circuit that functions as a maximum speed register. It compares a given speed input with its current output and updates the output to the higher value on each clock cycle, subject to an enable signal. The output resets to zero when the reset signal is activated. This design will reliably store and track the maximum speed encountered during operation.
module top_module(  clk, r, enable, speed,out
    );

code:
module top_module(  clk, r, enable, speed,out
    );parameter WIDTH = 7; 
    input [WIDTH-1:0]speed;
    input wire clk, r, enable;
    output reg [WIDTH-1:0] out = 0;

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (r) out <= 0;
        else if(enable == 1) out  <= (speed > out)? speed : out;
    end


endmodule

